{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/579126-demon-about-the-abyss-and-other-questions","id":579126,"title":"Demon: about the Abyss and other questions...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-04T14:18:10-07:00","id":579126,"title":"Demon: about the Abyss and other questions...","content":"Hello guys I have some questions for you:<br /> <br /> 1) Where I can learn more info about the Abyss? And what exactly is it? Just a empty space? Or something like a parallel world?<br /> <br /> 2) Even during the rebellion ages the fallen angels were in need for vessels to interact with humans?<br /> <br /> 3) During the rebellion against God, was plausible for fallen angels to craft futuristic weapons like beam sabers or droids?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T16:35:56-07:00","id":579254,"title":"","content":"1. Any Umbra book. What the Abyss is it's a Umbral Dimension that's pretty much like being in a oceanic trench minus the water.<br /> 2. I don't believe so since both sides didn't need vessels back in the day.<br /> 3. Possible, I can see that for a Descent to Fallen translation thing where those droids became Unchained Demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T17:11:22-07:00","id":579283,"title":"","content":"1) The Abyss is almost nothing. Almost without time, no space, just points of consciousness bunched up together, screaming and cursing each other.<br /> <br /> 2) The Fallen and Angels housed their beings in shells of Faith.<br /> <br /> 3) The Maelfactors did things like this in their chapter of Houses of the Fallen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 07-05-2015, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T17:48:03-07:00","id":579296,"title":"","content":"The Abyss is covered in a lot of sources, but its true nature never really explained. As much things in the WoD, each splat comprehend just a side of the question.<br /> <br /> I recomend you to look for books about the Umbra. Be aware that books meant to Werewolf and to Mage can have worlds of difference in what they say. Wraith have something to do with that, also, as the Abyss do have a manifestation in their world.<br /> <br /> And finally, anything of Vampire about the Lasombra clan. At the same time that, as most vampires, they are fairly ignorant of the Umbral Realms and Cosmology in general, they are also THE experts on the Abyss, mind you. This mix of knowledge and ignorance is a source of ideas about what the Abyss can be.<br /> <br /> Something lives there, by the way. Malicious but non-demonic stuff. And Demons seems to be completely unaware of their jailors. What are those things is anyones guess...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T18:58:55-07:00","id":579315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/579126-demon-about-the-abyss-and-other-questions#post579126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello guys I have some questions for you:<br /> <br /> 1) Where I can learn more info about the Abyss? And what exactly is it? Just a empty space? Or something like a parallel world?<br /> <br /> 2) Even during the rebellion ages the fallen angels were in need for vessels to interact with humans?<br /> <br /> 3) During the rebellion against God, was plausible for fallen angels to craft futuristic weapons like beam sabers or droids?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) Basically Nowhere other than the main books... \u201cThe oldest and strongest emotion of mankind is fear, and the oldest and strongest kind of fear is fear of the unknown\u201d <br /> Imagine, No..wait ..Try to imagine something that you Cant. A place fill with an almost alien level of Hate and Madness, Always thirsy, always hungry. ALWAYS feeling shouts of &quot;Youre Gulty.&quot;, A place where the sheer ammount of guilt and utter madness goes beyond the limits of the flesh and the mental pain. A place that forces you to Cannibalize yourself, to ALWAYS be afraid, and that slowly and painfully turns you inside out. Not a place, but also an idea, a concept that lies in your flesh and in your skin...The Rottening HATRED of the universe lying in your bones, and knowing that no matter how much you &quot;Scrub it off&quot; It will never, Ever..be enough. The Abysm its the most Eldritch Place in the WoD mythos, a place so Horrible, So..Utterly Evil and fill with pain and suffering that Demons are afraid of going back into it...And that (in my games at least) they envy humans and other supernaturals for not being able to process the mere thought of that place.<br /> On a game i played, my demon was fighting a serial killer and the killer tried to psycologically threat my demon. Crowley (my demon) only said &quot;You can show me the end of the world over and over, you can show me childs beeing mutilated, humanity beeing violated. you can show me the sheer horror of what your race is capable of...But that does not compare to a place made by the Hatred and Dissapointment of God.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) No, they were on their full &quot;Angelic&quot; Forms during their encounters. The Taking over the Flesh happend later on, when Fallen angels were turned inside out<br /> <br /> 3) On my game at least, No. <br /> Ok, lets get ready for some heavy discussions!!! * SPOILERS!*<br /> I belive that demons are limitated only to the &quot;First Order&quot; of things made during creation, that in a way &quot;Technology&quot; is perhaps too advanced or perhaps too &quot;Alien&quot; for them. NOW, this would also fit with the idea that Lucifer Awoke The Father of All and The Mother of All (since some belive that the Conciusness that humans have, is a human beeing awaken into a Mage). So, On that point of view, Technology is something that was forced upon the human world and something beyond the conception of demons (under the idea that now reality belongs to the technocracy and science).<br /> <br /> Returning to the subject, Could a Malefactor CREATE or rather Re Create Iluminated Science ? (Lasers, and Mechs?) Yes..And No.<br /> Yes, he could..As long He would be in the modern era.<br /> Not during the Original Rebelion..<br /> <br /> Remember, the keyword for a game like Demon the Fallen is the comprehention of being an Eldritch Horror <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T18:08:01-07:00","id":580412,"title":"","content":"Results may vary. Like so.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y-468WgS9To\" data-code=\"y-468WgS9To\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/y-468WgS9To/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T20:02:28-07:00","id":590721,"title":"","content":"1.) The Abyss doesn't exist. Its walls do, as a physical barrier where our world ends... and nothing extends beyond it. Anything you say about the abyss will probably be wrong because it doesn't exist. There is no space, no up no down no left no right. There are no lights, no sounds, no tastes, no touches. There is nowhere, and time does not exist within it as it does to us. Seconds and centuries are the same, yet thanks to a cruel fluke of the creator the consciousnesses of the fallen within can still continue to process. They are the only thing that exists within the pit: their will, their thoughts, and the faintest sounds of humanity just beyond the bars of their cell. Some poor souls would occasionally wander too close to the pit, and be snatched by sensory deprived demons intent on doing SOMETHING, ANYTHING! Those tortured souls became spectres, hunting through the tempest for other souls. Other powerful demons would struggle to project themselves into the nightmares of the living, while their fellow inmates would attempt to stop them from torturing their former charges.<br /> <br /> 2.) They were beings of pure faith, with physical manifestations created from their faith alone. If you look at page 90, Time of Judgement you'll find a sidebar that describes how Angels work, and should the world's ambient levels of faith progress to a level sufficient to sustain demons they too could exist without their mortal forms. It's kinda like oxygen. Without enough air in the room, you need a suit. Their human vessels are that suit. But also.... without tying themselves to a vessel the abyss would suck them in like a dust bunny down a vacuum cleaner. The Abyss would need to be destroyed before they could exist freely.<br /> <br /> 3.) Futuristic... sorta. They could produce blades of light and weapons that launched infernal hellfire or other terrible magical essences. They could create things that behaved like our technology appears to us, or like futuristic weaponry might look. Remember, any sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic. Surely, any sufficiently complex magic could mimic technology as well. It's just a difference of what systems underlay their operation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T00:21:33-07:00","id":591003,"title":"","content":"Can't say the Abyss don't exist. For one, there are Obtenebration, and a HUGE amount of evidence to its Abyss being the same of Demons. It can't be said for sure, but if true, hints to possible other denizens there. And given the sensory deprivation of trapped Demons, it IS possible that they where unable to perceive such &quot;jailers&quot;, instead of just alone.<br /> <br /> Such question don't have an easy unified answer. A lot of books from every WoD gameline have entries to things that can be the Abyss or not, and such entries can be true or biased. In the end, the ST is the one to really MAKE his own answer, with watever material he wants to use.<br /> <br /> And I do think Demons could make &quot;futuristic&quot; weaponry at the War, if you want to use it. They where the builders of the universe, there are no sense in thinking they couldn't envision the highest possible technology. They just knew every damn rule of nature or scientists are yet to even conceive of. At that time I would say that pretty much EVERYTHING was possible. I wouldn't use it, but possible? Yes, for sure!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T08:24:28-07:00","id":591354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/579126-demon-about-the-abyss-and-other-questions?p=591003#post591003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't say the Abyss don't exist. For one, there are Obtenebration, and a HUGE amount of evidence to its Abyss being the same of Demons. It can't be said for sure, but if true, hints to possible other denizens there. And given the sensory deprivation of trapped Demons, it IS possible that they where unable to perceive such &quot;jailers&quot;, instead of just alone</div> </div> </div> </div>It is an &quot;environment&quot; devoid of matter, energy, space, and time. It has no dimensions. It does not exist, in any sense which any living mind can conceive of it being either a place or a thing. The ability of vampires to bring forth shadows of that nothingness out into the world via obtenebration in no way precludes the possibility that the Abyss is nothingness. When I say the Abyss doesn't exist, I'm not saying there is no place that the fallen were cast into. I'm saying they were cast into literal nothingness. Language fails when you try to describe such a thing.<br /> <br /> &quot;The <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Lasombra_Antediluvian\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Antediluvian</a> sometimes claimed that the Abyss was the state of all creation before an interfering <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/God_%28cWOD%29\" target=\"_blank\">God</a> made light,&quot;<br /> <br /> The Abyss is actually shielded a bit from the primordial chaos that the creator shaped the world from. Earthbound can summon horrific creatures of madness from beyond the universe, things which live in that ever-shifting realm. The Abyss is less even than that place, being static.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T08:32:30-07:00","id":591363,"title":"","content":"I think there are actually several places called &quot;The Abyss.&quot; One is found in the mid umbra and it is supposed to be the maw of the Wyrm. The Abyss the Fallen were sentenced to is basically a Oblivion-lite. It feels like Oblivion but God made sure that the Fallen could survive the experience by making a little cage inside of it to keep the Fallen from being annhilated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T09:31:09-07:00","id":591402,"title":"","content":"I think the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Abyss_%28WTA%29\" target=\"_blank\">Abyss out of Werewolf</a> is a crack in the walls of the actual Abyss out of Demon, and falling deep enough into it will result in putting you in the same place. It results in sensory deprivation, it's a pit of non-existence, and it has a powerful pull that attracts spirits. All of these match up with the Abyss of Demon (also has some similarities to Oblivion). What the Werewolves call the Abyss is likely just the doorway to the actual Abyss that contains the Fallen, and the sensory deprivation they experience at its edges is just a taste of what demons suffer within.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Abyss_%28VTM%29\" target=\"_blank\">The Abyss mentioned in Vampire</a>, however, doesn't really seem to match up at all. They say it's totally uninhabited, other than a semi-sentience for the realm and the spirit of one of the vampires who died there. If they could detect their fellow vampire, they could surely detect the fallen. Which is odd.... because it totally contradicts comments about the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Baali\" target=\"_blank\">Baali</a>, who almost surely worship an Earthbound and are DEFINITELY connected to the right Abyss...<br /> <br /> It wouldn't take too much work on the part of the Storyteller to combine the Abyss of Demon, Vampire, &amp; Werewolf into being the same Abyss.<br /> <br /> As for Oblivion? Oblivion was a creation of the Slayers when they built their underworld, giving spirits a way out of existence should their afterlife become too much. Beneath <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Tempest\" target=\"_blank\">the Tempest</a> lies the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Labyrinth_%28WTO%29\" target=\"_blank\">Labyrinth</a>, a maddening descent into meaningless as one approaches the well of the void (I think it's one and the same as the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Black_Spiral_Labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">Black Spiral Labyrinth</a>). I can't find it now (it might be in one of my Demon books), but God crafted the Abyss at the heart of Oblivion (or just beneath it). Just to be a dick. He used the Dark Umbra (the construct which Demons named Haven, an artificial afterlife for the souls they were saving during the war) to construct their prison. Another thing I can't find right now is a mention of how Spectres are made. I swear I read that Spectres were the product of demons: that wraiths who strayed too far into Oblivion without being destroyed would find their way to the walls of the Abyss where demons scratching at their bars would grasp the spirit, pull it against the walls of reality and pervert the soul to its new form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T09:37:54-07:00","id":591406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/579126-demon-about-the-abyss-and-other-questions?p=591363#post591363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there are actually several places called &quot;The Abyss.&quot; One is found in the mid umbra and it is supposed to be the maw of the Wyrm. The Abyss the Fallen were sentenced to is basically a Oblivion-lite. It feels like Oblivion but God made sure that the Fallen could survive the experience by making a little cage inside of it to keep the Fallen from being annhilated.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wyrm is allegedly imprisoned in Malfeas, out in the Deep Umbra. The underworld, abyss, oblivion, tempest, and labyrinth is considered to be in the Dark Umbra, which is still here around-ish Earth, but beneath the other layers of the Umbra. The Black Spiral Labyrinth is also out in Malfeas in the Deep Umbra.<br /> <br /> But I don't subscribe to the notion of the Umbra as obeying Euclidean geometry. I think parts of it can wrap around, or fold over on itself, in perverse or convoluted ways. And things like Oblivion/The Abyss... they're the drain that all of reality could be slowly going down. All roads lead to Rome, as it were... I don't think you can escape such things, so no matter how far into the Deep Umbra you go it makes sense that you'd only find yourself coming to the end all over again.<br /> <br /> EDIT: dammit! LOL! Malfeas.... is in the Deep Umbra. Which is that big deep space of Umbra out beyond the solar system.<br /> <br /> ... it's also a <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Near_Realms\" target=\"_blank\">Near Realm</a>. Which means it's as close to us as the Abyss is. I'm going to call this as support for my non-Euclidean theory of the warped geography of the Umbra. Malfeas is both in the Deep Umbra and nearby, making the Black Spiral Labyrinth both distant and proximate (depending upon the road you take to reach it I suppose). So sure, the black spiral and the labyrinth of Wraith can be one and the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6883,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","user":"DarkExcalibur42","date":". 07-15-2015, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T15:14:25-07:00","id":591926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkExcalibur42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Oblivion? Oblivion was a creation of the Slayers when they built their underworld, giving spirits a way out of existence should their afterlife become too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>This it's a no-no for Slayers, as they didn't wanted to loss the Souls of humans. Actually, the Slayers never needed to create something to &quot;put out of existence&quot; the souls of humans because that was already happening (the souls of humans were lost, nobody knows where they were going, when humans died.). The Slayers wanted to keep the souls, never to &quot;end&quot; them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T17:43:26-07:00","id":592139,"title":"","content":"All those are viable explanations. By myself, I like to unify at least Vampire's and Demon's Abyss.<br /> <br /> But the point isn't about what the Abyss IS. There are no official answer to that. Its about what the Abyss CAN BE.<br /> <br /> Demons don't have an accurate answer to any property of the Abyss. They have a PERCEPTION of it. Not one I don't like, mind you. The point is, there are no guarantee about it being what they think. Or what anybody else think.<br /> <br /> High-level Obtenebration and Abyss Mysticism give you the power to summon weird phenomena from the Abyss. What are such phenomena? No one knows, and no official answer was given, ever. The vampire's soul shapes the shadow-stuff? Maybe. Those shadows are sentient beings? Maybe. Demons, or even stranger creatures? Maybe. Lots of maybes. The shadow-stuff could be made of psychic ectoplasm, manifested Torment, idiotified demons or something else entirely.<br /> <br /> It is up to the ST to define what the Abyss is in his game, and for sure those are all good ideas. But the only honest answer to the question 1 is: no one knows for sure, get a lot of books about what can be the Abyss or not and decide by yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T18:19:17-07:00","id":592158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/579126-demon-about-the-abyss-and-other-questions?p=591926#post591926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This it's a no-no for Slayers, as they didn't wanted to loss the Souls of humans. Actually, the Slayers never needed to create something to &quot;put out of existence&quot; the souls of humans because that was already happening (the souls of humans were lost, nobody knows where they were going, when humans died.). The Slayers wanted to keep the souls, never to &quot;end&quot; them.</div> </div> </div> </div>They did want to save human souls, and give them some place to rest. But what they wanted and what they could provide were not exactly the same. But you're right, I had part of this backwards.<br /> <br /> The Slayers built Haven. The creator ripped up the fabric of what was Haven, and used it to construct the Abyss (Houses of the Fallen 179). On this page, it also says that Charon tunneled out deeper and deeper into the void (this is the stuff of nonexistence that permeates all of the &quot;space&quot; outside of creation). But it does say that their world had a deathly palor cast over all of it, revealing a legacy of pain and making it an overall very grim place (p.177).<br /> <br /> I <i>thought</i> it said they built Oblivion (or built near Oblivion) because the nature of their existence was so imperfect, and souls who fatigued of their afterlife had a way out... but I don't see that. I must have mixed it up with something I read from Wraith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T18:39:38-07:00","id":592195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/579126-demon-about-the-abyss-and-other-questions#post579126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello guys I have some questions for you:<br /> <br /> 1) Where I can learn more info about the Abyss? And what exactly is it? Just a empty space? Or something like a parallel world?<br /> <br /> 2) Even during the rebellion ages the fallen angels were in need for vessels to interact with humans?<br /> <br /> 3) During the rebellion against God, was plausible for fallen angels to craft futuristic weapons like beam sabers or droids?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) rage across the heavens has a good entry on it<br /> <br /> 2) no, there was enough ambient faith that they could create their own bodies out of it, rules for this are in the earthbound book if I remember right<br /> <br /> 3) I don't see why not, you could have all kinds of things as part of their back story or flashbacks and there is no reason they couldn't make them now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T18:46:27-07:00","id":592200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/579126-demon-about-the-abyss-and-other-questions?p=579315#post579315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1) Basically Nowhere other than the main books... \u201cThe oldest and strongest emotion of mankind is fear, and the oldest and strongest kind of fear is fear of the unknown\u201d<br /> Imagine, No..wait ..Try to imagine something that you Cant. A place fill with an almost alien level of Hate and Madness, Always thirsy, always hungry. ALWAYS feeling shouts of &quot;Youre Gulty.&quot;, A place where the sheer ammount of guilt and utter madness goes beyond the limits of the flesh and the mental pain. A place that forces you to Cannibalize yourself, to ALWAYS be afraid, and that slowly and painfully turns you inside out. Not a place, but also an idea, a concept that lies in your flesh and in your skin...The Rottening HATRED of the universe lying in your bones, and knowing that no matter how much you &quot;Scrub it off&quot; It will never, Ever..be enough. The Abysm its the most Eldritch Place in the WoD mythos, a place so Horrible, So..Utterly Evil and fill with pain and suffering that Demons are afraid of going back into it...And that (in my games at least) they envy humans and other supernaturals for not being able to process the mere thought of that place.<br /> On a game i played, my demon was fighting a serial killer and the killer tried to psycologically threat my demon. Crowley (my demon) only said &quot;You can show me the end of the world over and over, you can show me childs beeing mutilated, humanity beeing violated. you can show me the sheer horror of what your race is capable of...But that does not compare to a place made by the Hatred and Dissapointment of God.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) No, they were on their full &quot;Angelic&quot; Forms during their encounters. The Taking over the Flesh happend later on, when Fallen angels were turned inside out<br /> <br /> 3) On my game at least, No.<br /> Ok, lets get ready for some heavy discussions!!! * SPOILERS!*<br /> I belive that demons are limitated only to the &quot;First Order&quot; of things made during creation, that in a way &quot;Technology&quot; is perhaps too advanced or perhaps too &quot;Alien&quot; for them. NOW, this would also fit with the idea that Lucifer Awoke The Father of All and The Mother of All (since some belive that the Conciusness that humans have, is a human beeing awaken into a Mage). So, On that point of view, Technology is something that was forced upon the human world and something beyond the conception of demons (under the idea that now reality belongs to the technocracy and science).<br /> <br /> Returning to the subject, Could a Malefactor CREATE or rather Re Create Iluminated Science ? (Lasers, and Mechs?) Yes..And No.<br /> Yes, he could..As long He would be in the modern era.<br /> Not during the Original Rebelion..<br /> <br /> Remember, the keyword for a game like Demon the Fallen is the comprehention of being an Eldritch Horror <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>the big thing to understand with demon is that everything is true on some level of creation or another<br /> <br /> and example would be the angelic army and demonic horde having a battle of the bands on one level while in another wielding the very living essence of the first tree as a weapons against each other. so yes, on some level of existence they could have been fighting in mechanized armors shooting lasers from their crotches and coming together to form a megazord or some such","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}